 on Center\nMANDATORY — production week. CALL TIME 9:30 AM: dancers mus
 t be checked in and backstage by then\, so arrive by 9:15 AM. BA: Call T
 ime is the time dancers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive 15 min
 utes before Call Time.\nACT I Student Matinee Performance (to recorded s
 ound)\; NO COFFEE\, BON BON\, ANGELS.\nAll Casts are called unless a cas
 t is named. SUBJECT TO CHANGE — the BA master schedule\, the weekly BA
  emails and the BA portal are the official source. Master: https://docs.
 google.com/spreadsheets/d/1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\
 n\nCOSTUME / HAIR / MAKEUP for Commandants: Soldiers: Commandant — Cos
 tume (you provide): Black Seamless Tights\, Black Camisole Leotard\; Sho
 es: Black Ballet Shoes\; Makeup: Men's Light Stage Makeup Light Stage Ma
 keup\; Hair: Male: Hair out of the eyes Female: High Bun\, No Part\; Acc
 essories (BA provides): White Gloves\; Prop (BA provides): White gun\nLi
 ght Stage Makeup Instruction Sheet:\n•  Powder matching skintone\n
 •  Light brown eye shadow applied to the crease with an eye shadow 
 brush\n•  Dark Brown/Black eyeliner and black mascara. No fake lash
 es.\n•  Blush on the cheeks (be sure to apply plenty so dancer does
 n’t look washed out in the stage lights)\n•  Red or Dark Red lips
 tick\nMen's Stage Makeup:\n•  Dark Brown/Black eyeliner - apply fro
 m corner to corner\n•  Brown or tan under cheek bone to create shad
 ow and accentuate the jaw line\n•  Brown eye liner around lips and 
 nude/flesh colored lipstick\n• *Men will not look like they are wearin
 g makeup. It will help the face be seen from the stage.\nDancers of Colo
 r may wear flesh tone tights and flesh tone ballet shoes.\nCostume Care 
 Guidelines:\n•  Handle costume pieces with care while changing to p
 revent damage to delicate fabrics\n•  Promptly notify Ballet Arkans
 as in the event of costume damage at the point of discovery\, no matter 
 how significant\n•  Never throw costumes or accessories on the floo
 r\, or hang costumes by their elastic straps\n•  Refrain from sitti
 ng on the floor while in costume\n•  Do not attempt to alter\, mend
 \, clean\, or launder any costume or accessory\n•  Never apply stag
 e make-up while in costume and shall take great care to refrain from smu
 dging make-up on costume during its removal\n•  Refrain from the us
 e of spray perfume or cologne while in costume\n•  Never wear any g
 arment not assigned to cast member\n•  Do not handle or consume foo
 d or beverage while in costume\, with the exception of water\n•  Do
  not remove costumes from their assigned dressing rooms or from the thea
 ter\n•  Remove all bobby pins used to secure head pieces and wigs f
 ollowing their use\n•  Return all headpieces to their assigned bags
 \n•  Comply fully with any and all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ wa
 rdrobe policies\n•  Do not pack markers\, paints\, colored drinks o
 r anything that may damage or stain costumes.
